#### Rust `network/` Module — Versioned Envelopes

##### [NEW] `src-tauri/src/network/envelope.rs`
- Define `SignedEnvelope<T>` struct:
  ```rust
  pub struct SignedEnvelope<T: Serialize> {
      pub v: u8,        // always 2
      pub msg_type: String,
      pub id: String,
      pub author: String,
      pub community_id: String,
      pub timestamp: String,
      pub payload: T,
      pub signature: String,
  }
  ```
- `SignedEnvelope::sign(identity, payload) -> Self`.
- `SignedEnvelope::verify(&self) -> Result<bool>` — uses `crypto::identity::verify_signature`.
- Typed payload variants: `MessagePayload`, `ReactionPayload`, `FileAnnouncedPayload`, `PresencePayload`, `KeyRotationPayload`, `CommunityControlPayload`, `HistoryResponsePayload`.
- All user-visible fields (`authorDisplayName`, `authorAvatarColor`, file metadata, reaction verb, moderation metadata) **must be inside the signed payload**, not as top-level unsigned fields.

##### [MODIFY] [app_runtime.rs](file:///c:/Users/dhawa/Desktop/Creations/Applications/Mesh/mesh/src-tauri/src/app_runtime.rs)
- **Critical change:** If a community has a stored group key, any message that fails decryption is **rejected** (dropped + logged), never parsed as plaintext. Currently `try_decrypt_community_payload` returns `None` on failure and the code falls through to plaintext parsing (line 95-96).
- Replace loose `serde_json::Value` envelope parsing with `SignedEnvelope::from_bytes()` deserialization + `verify()` call. Removes ~200 lines of manual field extraction.
- Unify the verification pipeline: extract a `validate_and_route(envelope: SignedEnvelope<Value>)` function used by both gossipsub messages **and** `MessageHistoryReceived` responses. History responses are currently trusted without re-validation (lines 517-523).
- Add SHA-256 file hash verification after completed downloads (in `DownloadUpdate::Completed` handler, lines 485-494).

##### [MODIFY] [behaviour.rs](file:///c:/Users/dhawa/Desktop/Creations/Applications/Mesh/mesh/src-tauri/src/network/behaviour.rs)
